* ECE334 ngspice defaults.
*
* Selected by SPICE_USERINIT_DIR in common/.designinit.
*
* The container ships SPICE_USERINIT_DIR pointing at the IHP SG13G2 PDK, whose
* .spiceinit preloads Verilog-A (OSDI) compact models from
* $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi.  Once PDK=sky130A that path does not
* exist -- SKY130 uses ngspice's built-in BSIM models and ships no OSDI -- so
* every simulation printed eight "couldn't be loaded" errors before doing the
* right thing anyway.  Pointing SPICE_USERINIT_DIR here removes the noise.

* Match the machine, but leave a core for the GUI.
set num_threads=4

* HSPICE-compatible parsing: the SKY130 model files use "nf" alongside "W".
set ngbehavior=hsa

* Skip redundant model checks; noticeably faster on the SKY130 corner libraries.
set ng_nomodcheck

* SKY130 models behavioural resistors; keep their noise contribution.
set enable_noisy_r
